    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-17" id="fn-17" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Transferred to Account No. 211, Miscellaneous Paid-in Capital.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-18" id="fn-18" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Transferred to Account No. 211, Miscellaneous Paid-in Capital.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-19" id="fn-19" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">General Plant reported does not include an allocation of corporate facilities to or from Tallgrass Energy Partners, LP ("TEP") and affiliates.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-20" id="fn-20" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">The provisions of Codification Topic 980, "Regulated Operation," (Unamortized AFUDC in Plant) authorized in the FERC's Accounting Guidance issued April 23, 1993 in Docket No. AI93-5-000 - Accounting for Income Taxes. Regulatory asset additions for Topic 980 are based on balances in Construction Work in Progress (Account 107). The period of amortization for the Equity AFUDC regulatory asset balances correlates to depreciation rates of the property, plant and equipment of 2.86%.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-21" id="fn-21" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Represents under collections pursuant to the REX tariff fuel/power tracker mechanisms.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-22" id="fn-22" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Represents under collections pursuant to the REX tariff fuel/power tracker mechanisms.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-23" id="fn-23" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Represents the Annual Charge Adjustment ("ACA"), which is an annual fee charged by the FERC and recovered from the shippers.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-24" id="fn-24" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Penalty charges are refundable based upon Section 37 of the REX Tariff and FERC's Order No. 637 rules.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-25" id="fn-25" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Pursuant to Docket No. RP11-1844, et al, this represents a reserve for refund for the period from April 2011 through December 2015.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-26" id="fn-26" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Represents over collections pursuant to the REX tariff fuel/power tracker mechanisms.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-27" id="fn-27" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">In accordance with the Tax Cuts and Jobs Act signed into law on December 22, 2017, REX remeasured its accumulated deferred income taxes (Accounts 190, 282, and 283) based on the new tax rates, resulting in a decrease in the net deferred tax liability. The adjustment was recorded in Account 254. The balance is amortized to Account 410.1, Provision of Deferred Income Taxes, over the estimated remaining useful life of the pipeline.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-28" id="fn-28" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Park and loan service volumes reported net: 75,197 dth</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-29" id="fn-29" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Park and loan service volumes reported net: (101,343) dth</link:footnote>
