    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-31" id="fn-31" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Fuel recovery volumes (shipper supplied gas for transmission): 1,614,600 dth</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-32" id="fn-32" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Fuel recovery volumes (shipper supplied gas for transmission): 1,300,434 dth</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-33" id="fn-33" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Fuel recovery volumes (shipper supplied gas for transmission): 1,609,353 dth</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-34" id="fn-34" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">The electric power cost used in compressor station operations was $12,929,434</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-35" id="fn-35" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Many of the natural gas volumes required to be reported on this page are tracked at the entity level, rather than by service type (i.e. firm transport, interruptible transport, etc.) or by discounted, negotiated, or recourse rate contracts and, therefore, the amounts reported have been allocated to the service types and to discounted, negotiated or recourse rate contracts based on reasonable assumptions.</link:footnote>
